    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Does video content really matter on LinkedIn for Founders + CEOs + MDs?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Yes — LinkedIn's algorithm heavily prioritizes video in 2026. Native video posts reach 3-5x more people than text-only posts for Founder/CEO, Managing Director, Chief Executive, Co-founder, Executive Chairman, Second-generation family-business CEO. LinkedIn Reels (30-90 sec vertical video) get 2-4x further reach than standard videos. For Founders + CEOs + MDs, video content covering Company vision + strategy + team + culture + fund-raising + hiring milestones + customer wins + industry-thesis + long-form founder-brand essays drives massive brand-recall + inbound. Even 1-2 short videos per month meaningfully lifts overall LinkedIn performance.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What kind of video content works for Founders + CEOs + MDs?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Winning formats: (1) Trending audio + industry commentary — 30-90 sec Reels riding trending sounds. (2) Talking-head insight — you on camera explaining a framework/trend/insight in 60-180 sec. (3) Behind-the-scenes — office/plant/site visit content. (4) Whiteboard/screen recording — explaining a chart/data/concept. (5) Interview clips — you interviewing a peer or being interviewed. (6) Client testimonial (with consent) — 60-90 sec client sharing outcomes. For Founder/CEO, Managing Director, Chief Executive, Co-founder, Executive Chairman, Second-generation family-business CEO, all these work. Video does NOT need Hollywood production — smartphone quality is acceptable.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we produce LinkedIn video content as a busy founder or CEO?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">3 workflows: (1) Batch record — 60-90 min monthly session, record 8-12 videos back-to-back. ITD editor cuts to 8-12 individual Reels/videos. (2) In-context capture — record 60-second clips before/after client meetings or during travel. Send to ITD via WhatsApp. Editor cleans + adds captions. (3) Interview format — ITD conducts 30-min recorded interview quarterly, edits to 4-6 Reels + 1 long-form video. Time investment: 60-90 min/month for the founder or CEO. Everything else handled by ITD (Premium tier).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">Do we need professional video production for LinkedIn?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">No — LinkedIn users prefer authentic smartphone-shot video over over-produced content. Requirements: (1) Well-lit (natural light from window or ring-light). (2) Clear audio (Bluetooth mic or Airpods mic beats built-in phone mic). (3) Landscape or vertical (depending on Reel vs standard video). (4) Captions burned-in (85% of LinkedIn video is watched with sound off — always add captions). (5) Under 90 seconds for Reels, under 3 minutes for standard video. ITD's Growth + Premium tiers include video editing, captioning, and thumbnail creation.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is LinkedIn Live + when to use it as founder or CEO?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">LinkedIn Live is broadcast-style live video (30-60 min sessions). Requires Creator Mode + 150+ followers. For Founder/CEO, Managing Director, Chief Executive, Co-founder, Executive Chairman, Second-generation family-business CEO, LinkedIn Live works for: (1) Q&A sessions on industry topics. (2) Interview/panel with peer expert. (3) Market update commentary (weekly/monthly). (4) Client webinar (broadcast to LinkedIn audience simultaneously). Well-promoted senior professionals draw 500-5,000+ live viewers + 30-100 booked meetings per session. ITD's Premium + Enterprise tiers include LinkedIn Live production support (streaming setup, teleprompter, editing to Reels).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does LinkedIn Reels differ from standard LinkedIn video?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">LinkedIn Reels (launched 2024-2025): vertical 9:16 format, 30-90 seconds, algorithmically pushed to non-followers via a dedicated Reels feed. Standard LinkedIn video: horizontal 16:9 or square 1:1, up to 10 minutes, shown primarily to your existing network. For Founders + CEOs + MDs, mix: 60-70% Reels (best for reach + follower growth) + 20-30% standard video (best for depth + LinkedIn Live archive) + 10% long-form (5-10 min for deep-dives).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What video content mistakes do Founders + CEOs + MDs make?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Corporate-lecture tone — LinkedIn Reels reward authentic + conversational. (2) No captions — 85% of viewers watch with sound off. (3) Weak first 3 seconds — LinkedIn algorithm drops videos with weak retention early. (4) Over 3 minutes for Reels format (Reels cap at 90 sec). (5) Vertical/horizontal format mismatch (Reels must be 9:16). (6) No CTA at end — where should viewers go next? (7) Recording in noisy environment (bad audio kills). (8) Poor lighting (dim/backlit video).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How much video content should a founder or CEO post?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For Founders + CEOs + MDs at Growth tier: 2-4 videos/Reels per month. Premium tier: 4-8 videos/month + 1 LinkedIn Live/quarter. Enterprise tier: 6-15 videos + monthly LinkedIn Live + weekly newsletter-supporting video clips. Video velocity + consistency matter more than production polish — algorithm rewards regular posting.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we caption LinkedIn videos?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Two options: (1) Burned-in captions (subtitles hardcoded into video) — required for maximum reach. (2) LinkedIn's auto-caption feature (SRT upload) — accessible but doesn't display in silent-scroll. Best practice: burn-in captions for Reels + short video (max reach). Use auto-caption for LinkedIn Live + long-form (accessibility + searchability). ITD's video editors use tools like CapCut, Descript, or Rev to generate + burn-in professional captions.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What LinkedIn Reels trends work for Founders + CEOs + MDs?</h2>
